<% content_for :title, "Home" %>
<%= render "tabs", tab: "home" %>

<h1 class="visually-hidden">Anti-Capitalist Community Auction</h1>

<% if admin_signed_in? %>
  <p class="mt-3 d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    <%= link_to "New Item", new_item_path,
        { class: "btn btn-default bg-danger-subtle" } %>
    <%= link_to "Upload CSV", new_items_csv_path,
        { class: "btn btn-default bg-danger-subtle" } %>
    <%= link_to "New User", new_user_path,
        { class: "btn btn-default bg-danger-subtle" } %>
    <%= link_to "Site Settings", site_settings_path,
        { class: "btn btn-default bg-danger-subtle" } %>
    <%= link_to "Award", awards_path,
        { class: "btn btn-default bg-danger-subtle" } %>
  </p>
<% end %>

<br/>

<p>
  As a participant in the event, you have 500 hearts to use
  <% if auction_items? || unlimited_items? %>
    across the kinds of items below. Each kind works a little differently:
  <% else %>
    on raffle items.
  <% end %>
</p>

<% if unlimited_items? %>
  <% costs = Item.unlimited_costs %>
  <p>
    <b><%= link_to "Unlimited Items:", items_path(type: 'Unlimited') %></b>
    These items have their own tab and no participation limit, so
    everyone who signs up gets one.
    <% if costs.one? %>
      Each one costs <%= pluralize(costs.first, "heart") %>.
    <% else %>
      They cost between <%= costs.first %> and
      <%= pluralize(costs.last, "heart") %>, as shown on each listing.
    <% end %>
    If you sign up for one of these items, you are guaranteed a spot
    at the event for you and a plus one, or you and your family.
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  <b><%= link_to "Raffle Items:", items_path %></b>
  Choose how many hearts you would like to enter for each item. Many
  items have multiple winners. Raffle winners will be drawn after the
  event has concluded and notified via email. The
  <% if admin_signed_in? || limited_bidding_allowed? %>
    Fairy Helper (below) is the easiest way to spread your hearts over
    these items.
  <% else %>
    Raffle Drawing Strategy section below explains how the hearts you
    enter turn into winners.
  <% end %>
</p>

<% if auction_items? %>
  <p>
    <b><%= link_to "Auction:", items_path(type: 'Auction') %></b>
    These items will be auctioned live during the event (see details
    below). You can view the item listings before the auction starts.
  </p>
<% end %>

<% if admin_signed_in? || limited_bidding_allowed? %>
  <p>
    <b><%= link_to "Fairy Helper:", ranking_path %></b>
    Rather than deciding how many hearts to put on each raffle item,
    you can put the raffle items in the order you want them and let the
    Auction Fairy spread your hearts across the list, with the most
    hearts on your top choice.
  </p>
<% end %>

<br/>

<h2 class="h4">Website Navigation:</h2>

<p>
  <b>To view items</b>, select the corresponding tab at the top of the
  page. On the Raffle Items tab, click Filter by Tag to see only items
  falling into a particular category.
</p>

<p>
  <b>To view item details</b>, including item description, host,
  accessibility information, and timing, select the Enter Hearts
  button to the right of an item.
</p>

<% if admin_signed_in? || limited_bidding_allowed? %>
  <p>
    <b>To enter hearts with the Fairy Helper</b>, select the Fairy
    Helper tab, type in <b>your unique code</b>, and click Continue.
    Use the heart buttons to add every raffle item you have any
    interest in to your list, then move your favorites toward the top.
    Click an item's name to see its details. When you click Save, your
    hearts are spread across your list, with the most hearts on the
    item at the top, and you are told how many hearts are left
    over. You can come back and rearrange your list as often as you
    like while raffle entries are open. Saving replaces any hearts you
    had entered on raffle items<% if unlimited_items? %>, but it
    leaves your unlimited items alone<% end %>.
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  <b>To enter hearts on a single item</b>, open the item and write in
  <b>your unique code</b> and the number of hearts you want to enter.
  This number will be deducted from your total. <b>To change the
  number of hearts</b> you want for a certain item, type in your code
  and the <b>total number of hearts</b> you want, then click the
  "Update Hearts" button. (For example, if you have already entered 10
  hearts, and you want to add 5 more, type in 15 total. If you type in
  5, you will only enter 5.)  If you want to remove all of your hearts
  from an item, type in your code, enter 0 hearts, and click "Update
  Hearts."
</p>

<% if unlimited_items? %>
  <p>
    Note: For items on the <b>Unlimited</b> tab, type in your code,
    check the "Get One" box, and click "Update Hearts." The cost shown
    on the item will be deducted from your total. To remove yourself
    from an unlimited item, type in your code, un-check the "Get One"
    box, and click "Update Hearts."
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  <b>To view your heart balance</b>, select the Users tab and find
  your name. <b>Click on your name</b> to see how many hearts you
  have spent on each item.
</p>

<br/>

<% if auction_items? %>
  <h2 class="h4">Auction:</h2>
  <p>
    During the auction, each item will be announced, and you will have a
    chance to bid. The item will go to the highest individual bidder,
    who will have deducted the number of hearts they bid. The amount you
    bid is part of your total heart count. Please do not bid more than
    you have.
  </p>
<% end %>

<% hearts_start = SiteSetting.next_limited_bidding_enable_time %>
<% hearts_end = SiteSetting.limited_bidding_end_time %>
<% site_end = SiteSetting.site_end_time %>

<h2 class="h4">Deadlines:</h2>

<p>
  <% if hearts_start %>
    Entering hearts on raffle items opens
    <b><%= event_time(hearts_start) %></b><% if hearts_end && hearts_end > hearts_start %>
      and closes <b><%= event_time(hearts_end) %></b><% end %>.
  <% elsif limited_bidding_allowed? && hearts_end %>
    Raffle items are available for entering hearts until
    <b><%= event_time(hearts_end) %></b>.
  <% elsif limited_bidding_allowed? %>
    Raffle items are available for entering hearts until the event is
    over.
  <% elsif hearts_end && hearts_end <= Time.current %>
    Raffle items closed for entering hearts on
    <b><%= event_time(hearts_end) %></b>.
  <% else %>
    Raffle items are not currently available for entering hearts.
  <% end %>
  <% if unlimited_items? %>
    <% if site_end && hearts_end && site_end > hearts_end %>
      Items on the <b>Unlimited</b> tab stay open until
      <b><%= event_time(site_end) %></b>, so any hearts left over when
      the raffle items close can still go there.
    <% elsif site_end %>
      Items on the <b>Unlimited</b> tab stay open until
      <b><%= event_time(site_end) %></b>.
    <% else %>
      Items on the <b>Unlimited</b> tab stay open for as long as the
      site is up.
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</p>

<p>
  Thank you for your participation! We could not do the work we do
  without your support.
</p>

<h2 class="h4">Raffle Drawing Strategy</h2>

<p>
  In keeping with the anti-capitalist, community-centered spirit of
  this event, we are using a modified approach to drawing raffle
  winners. You can read more about our algorithm below, but the short
  version is: we’re making it more likely that everyone who
  participates will win something! To increase your chances of winning
  the items you want, we suggest using the following strategy:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>Put at least 1 heart on every item you are interested in.</li>

  <li>
    Put the most hearts on the item you are most interested in. Then,
    put the second-most hearts on the item you are second-most
    interested in, and so on. (For example: If you have 100 hearts
    and are interested in 3 items, you might put 50 hearts on your
    first choice, 30 on your second choice, and 20 on your third
    choice.)
  </li>
</ul>

<p>
  <% if admin_signed_in? || limited_bidding_allowed? %>
    The Fairy Helper does this for you: everything on your list gets at
    least 1 heart, and the hearts count down from your top choice.
    Items near the bottom of your list do not take anything away from
    the ones above them, so add everything you have any interest in.
    If you would rather do it by hand, start by going through the list
    of raffle items and adding 1 heart to every item you are interested
    in. Then, look at the list of items you have put hearts on, and add
    more to your favorites until all your remaining hearts are
    distributed.
  <% else %>
    One way to do this is to start by going through the list of raffle
    items and adding 1 heart to every item you are interested in. Then,
    look at the list of items you have put hearts on, and add more to
    your favorites until all your remaining hearts are distributed.
  <% end %>
</p>

<h3 class="h4">The Algorithm</h3>
<p>
  To maximize the chances of everyone winning at least one item they
  are interested in, we are using an algorithm to choose winners
  rather than doing a simple random heart draw. The algorithm works
  in the following way:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>One participant is randomly selected.<sup>*</sup></li>
  <li>The selected participant is assigned the item that they placed the most hearts on.
    <ul>
      <li>If that item is no longer available, they are assigned the item they placed the second-most hearts on, and so on.</li>
      <li>
	If they placed the same number of hearts on two items, they are assigned whichever item has the fewest total hearts from
	all participants.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
    The process repeats until all items are assigned or there are no
    participants left who want the remaining items.
  </li>
</ul>

<sup>*</sup>Note: the random selection is technically a shuffle of
all the participants, so no one gets two items before everyone has at
least had a chance to get their first time.  Once everyone gets a
chance to get something, the list of participants is again shuffled.
